**** MAC USERS PLEASE TAKE NOTE!!!

the mac version of nethack, nh30j3(+), at linc.cis.upenn.edu (dated
Jul. '91) requires 1.5M in one implementation and only 800k in its
other implementation.  this is different than the originally released
versions of mac nethack which in one version required 3M.  the 1.5M
version (distinguished by its use of 'vers' resources) is recommended,
as it was found to work on all macs (at that time) running all current
system software (6.0.x or 7.0.x).  the same cannot be said for the other
versions or implementations of mac nethack, which were known to have
problems.  btw, the display for the recommended version should be quick
even without caching and ram disks, etc.

[] Programming nerd aside:
