for different reasons, a bug crept into the memory management on the
mac port.  the "fix" was to use basic memory management: place all
segments into memory at once and never unload anything!

the mac port for the next version of nethack (3.1) is an even more
difficult chore.  interested, willing and _able_ mac hackers should
come to the front if they would like to see that mac nethack 3.1
gets built right.  not all offers will be accepted, etc. ...

please note that i am _not_ authorized to speak on behalf of the
mac dev team or the general nethack dev team.  still, i think they
might appreciate a helping hand, preferably from someone who has
built 3.0 and is somewhat familiar with nethack code, in general.

